; this archive's record drawer: its manifest and options (below), its VERSIONS (for an
; Update's two version lines) and a copy of its Uninstall, which the base's Uninstall runs
MakeDir >NIL: @PKGDIR@ @RECORD@
Copy VERSIONS @RECORDP@VERSIONS CLONE QUIET
; the Uninstall sits beside this Files drawer. Never as /Uninstall: UnixDirs3 UNIXROOT
; reads a leading / as the root, /Uninstall as the volume Uninstall: (a "Please insert
; volume" requester). Nor as UPTFILES:/Uninstall: C:Copy 47.7 splits that into a lock on
; UPTFILES: plus the relative name /Uninstall, again the root (rc 20, IoErr 218 "device
; (or volume) is not mounted"). No name handed to Copy, Delete, Rename etc may be NAME:/...;
; only Assign locks the whole X:/ name. So an assign on the current drawer (whatever form
; DIR has: Files, UPTKIT:, a path with a trailing /) gets a second assign on its parent,
; and Copy names UPTPARENT:Uninstall.
Assign >NIL: UPTFILES: ""
Assign >NIL: UPTPARENT: UPTFILES:/
Copy UPTPARENT:Uninstall @RECORDP@Uninstall CLONE QUIET
Assign >NIL: UPTPARENT:
Assign >NIL: UPTFILES:
